    "result_text": "The full test suite passes. The three test files are `AcceptanceTest` (the only actual test class) plus its support classes `AcceptanceBase` and `AuditLogCapture`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the welcome-notification enqueue on successful owner create in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n1. **Added a dedicated `NOTIFY` logger** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:88`) alongside the existing `AUDIT` logger, matching the codebase convention of a named, static logger for side-effect checkpoints.\n\n2. **Added `enqueueWelcomeNotification(Owner)`** which emits a single line on the `NOTIFY` logger containing the owner's id and `memberId`.\n\n3. **Wired it into the create flow** in `createOwner(...)`, right after the audit step \u2014 so it fires only on a successful create (after all validation/dedup rejections and the persist), keeping the pipeline reading as \"make the owner, audit it, then welcome it.\"\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` passes: it captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts a line contains both the owner id and the memberId. `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
